## Story Description
Add two GET endpoints to backend/app/routers/ingestion.py. GET /batches returns all ingestion batches for the engagement ordered newest-first. GET /batches/{batch_id} returns batch metadata plus a pipeline_status breakdown from transactions_raw and the first 25 raw rows. Both follow the existing text()/conn.execute()/verify_engagement_ownership() pattern in the same file.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: backend/app/routers/ingestion.py — add GET endpoint at path /batches (full path: /api/engagements/{engagement_id}/ingest/batches). Query: SELECT id, filename, row_count, new_rows, duplicate_rows, status, uploaded_at, completed_at FROM ingestion_batches WHERE engagement_id = :eid ORDER BY uploaded_at DESC NULLS LAST. Returns list of dicts. Uses verify_engagement_ownership() and engine = Depends(_engine).
- Edit file: backend/app/routers/ingestion.py — add GET endpoint at path /batches/{batch_id}. First verify the batch belongs to the engagement (SELECT engagement_id FROM ingestion_batches WHERE id = :bid; raise 404 if not found, 403 if wrong engagement). Return dict with: batch (all columns from ingestion_batches), pipeline_status_breakdown (SELECT pipeline_status, COUNT(*) as count FROM transactions_raw WHERE batch_id=:bid GROUP BY pipeline_status), sample_rows (SELECT id, invoice_number, invoice_date, raw_supplier_name, base_amount, pipeline_status FROM transactions_raw WHERE batch_id=:bid ORDER BY created_at ASC LIMIT 25).
- Run: cd backend && python -c "from app.routers.ingestion import router; routes=[r.path for r in router.routes]; print(routes)" — output should contain strings ending in '/batches' and '/batches/{batch_id}'

